---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../content/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Information about the inquiry form, the data it asks for, and the privacy details required before launch."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">A thoughtful approach to your information</p>
      <h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1>
    </section>
    <div class="prose">
      {site.approvals.privacy && site.privacyText ? (
        <p>{site.privacyText}</p>
      ) : (
        <>
          <aside class="review-notice">
            <p>
              Prelaunch note. Inquiry submission is turned off while the privacy policy is
              finalized. The final notice requires verified provider settings, retention limits, a
              deletion process, and a public contact address. See the{' '}
              <a href="/launch-checklist/">launch checklist</a>.
            </p>
          </aside>
          <h2>Only what helps with your inquiry.</h2>
          <p>
            The proposed form asks for your name, email, interest, and a short description. A
            category-specific follow-up is optional. Do not send sensitive business information,
            passwords, payment details, or client records.
          </p>
          <h2>How inquiries would be handled.</h2>
          <p>
            Formspree is the selected form provider. Before launch, the owner must verify provider
            storage, notification delivery, free-plan limits, and deletion procedures for both the
            provider dashboard and email inbox.
          </p>
          <h2>Retention and deletion.</h2>
          <p>
            The retention period and deletion contact are not yet approved. No permanent archive,
            automatic acknowledgment, or durable CRM is promised.
          </p>
          <h2>No analytics at launch.</h2>
          <p>
            The site does not include analytics, advertising trackers, or an AI chat widget. The
            proposed form keeps inquiry contents out of URLs, browser storage, and application logs.
          </p>
        </>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
